messages:
Alex W: Heads-up — running into an annoying issue when using redwood-sdk-js in an edge function inside our pnpm monorepo. Vercel Edge throws a runtime resolution/exports error: `The requested module ... does not provide an export named 'default'`. Works when I bundle locally. Anyone hit weird ESM/CJS + pnpm workspace hoisting + edge runtime interaction? :thinking_face:

Maria G: Can you paste the sdk package.json (packages/redwood-sdk-js)? Need to see "main", "module", "exports", "types".

Alex W: Trimmed package.json from packages/redwood-sdk-js:

```json
{
  "name": "redwood-sdk-js",
  "version": "0.12.0-next",
  "main": "dist/cjs/index.js",
  "module": "dist/esm/index.mjs",
  "types": "dist/types/index.d.ts",
  "exports": {
    ".": {
      "require": "./dist/cjs/index.js",
      "import": "./dist/esm/index.mjs"
    }
  }
}
```

Chris L: That exports map is reasonable. Edge runtimes expect an ESM entrypoint and pnpm symlinks can confuse the runtime's package boundary resolution. Two things: 1) are you importing `import SDK from 'redwood-sdk-js'` or a subpath? 2) verify the deploy artifact actually includes `dist/esm/index.mjs`.

Alex W: We do `import { Client } from 'redwood-sdk-js'` in the edge file. Deploy zip includes `node_modules/redwood-sdk-js/dist/esm/index.mjs` under the .pnpm tree. Error indicates the runtime can't find exported names.

Karthik R: pnpm uses symlinks; Node ESM resolution is strict about package boundaries. Workarounds: publish an explicit ESM-only entry for edge (e.g. `exports.edge`) and import `redwood-sdk-js/edge`, or ship a root-level ESM re-export so the runtime sees a package root ESM file not behind a symlink.

Sam T: Example dual exports with edge entry:

```json
"exports": {
  ".": {
    "types": "./dist/types/index.d.ts",
    "import": "./dist/esm/index.mjs",
    "require": "./dist/cjs/index.js"
  },
  "./edge": {
    "import": "./dist/edge/index.mjs"
  }
}
```

Also add top-level "types" for TS.

Maria G: Short-term pnpm hack: set `shamefully-hoist=true` in .npmrc during the build to flatten deps, or use `public-hoist-pattern` to hoist redwood-sdk-js. Not ideal for customers. Long-term: publish dedicated edge entry that doesn't rely on hoisting.

Alex W: I don't want to force hoisting. I'll add `./edge` and an ESM wrapper that re-exports minimal runtime code. Would `import { Client } from 'redwood-sdk-js/edge'` work with Vercel bundlers?

Chris L: Yes. Include a `.mjs` wrapper and ensure package.json points to it in `exports`. Example wrapper (dist/edge/index.mjs):

```js
// wrapper that re-exports ESM-friendly symbols
export { Client } from '../esm/index.mjs';
```

Karthik R: For TS in workspaces, add `typesVersions` to map to dist types for subpath imports, e.g.:

```json
"typesVersions": { "*": { "*": ["dist/types/*"] } }
```

Alex W: Added ./edge export and pushed a patch build. Deploy still failed; stack shows the edge runtime resolving from the symlinked .pnpm path and picking the CJS build.

Sam T: Check the consumer build/bundler. Some bundlers or esbuild configs can force require() of CJS. We added a resolve alias to force the edge import to the distributed mjs in our Next.js config:

```js
// next.config.js
module.exports = {
  webpack: (config) => {
    config.resolve.alias['redwood-sdk-js/edge'] = path.resolve(__dirname, 'node_modules/redwood-sdk-js/dist/edge/index.mjs');
    return config;
  }
}
```

Maria G: Repro test: create a minimal project outside the monorepo (npm install redwood-sdk-js) and deploy the same edge file. If that works, it's definitely pnpm workspace layout.

Alex W: Repro outside monorepo worked — confirmed pnpm/workspace. I'll try `shamefully-hoist` in CI for now and open a PR to publish a dedicated edge entry that avoids symlink issues.

pkg-bot: Internal release 0.12.0-next.1 with ./edge export pushed to internal registry at 1712001300.

Alex W: Thanks all, follow-up PR and CI link incoming. Saved me a day. :relieved:

Chris L: When you open the PR, add a CI test that imports `redwood-sdk-js/edge` in a Vercel Edge job.

Karthik R: Also add a README note about pnpm pitfalls and recommended exports layout.

Sam T: If types don't resolve for `/edge`, ping me — we can add typesVersions and a tiny declaration file that re-exports types.

Alex W: Will do.
